The   same construction of Sections~\ref{s:3} and~\ref{s:4}  also yields consequences when one allows non-injective maps.  The reason is that one may add dummy generators without changing the large subgroup already lying in the equalizer.

\begin{prop}\label{prop:one-noninj}
For every integer $r\ge 5$, there exist homomorphisms
% \[
